### HIGH: gemini (gemini-code-assist[bot])
**File**: `scripts/npm-postinstall.cjs:33`
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `log` function does not handle potential errors from `fs.writeSync()`. If writing to the TTY fails (e.g., the terminal is closed during script execution), the script will crash, and subsequent log messages will not be displayed. This could prevent the user from seeing important installation instructions.

To make the script more robust, I suggest adding error handling. If a write fails, the script should close the TTY file descriptor, set it to `null`, and fall back to using `process.stderr` for the current and all subsequent log messages.

```
const log = (msg = '') => {
    const line = msg + '\n';
    if (ttyFd !== null) {
        try {
            fs.writeSync(ttyFd, line);
        } catch {
            // TTY write failed. Fall back to stderr for this and subsequent calls.
            try { fs.closeSync(ttyFd); } catch { /* best effort to close */ }
            ttyFd = null;
            process.stderr.write(line);
        }
    } else {
        process.stderr.write(line);
    }
};
```

